 out the decryption key. Commander Kael placed the decryption key on the tactical console with a distinct clatter. Captain Maria . watched the decryption key carefully; the decryption key's presence was vital for the upcoming nebula navigation.\n\nAn hour later, they descended to the Medical Bay to check on the wounded from the last skirmish. Dr. Aris was waiting for them by the stasis pods, looking weary.\n\n\"Report, Dr. Aris,\" Captain Maria . commanded.\n\n\"The patient is stable, Captain,\" Dr. Aris replied, adjusting Dr. Aris's glasses.\n\nCaptain Maria . nodded. \"Good work, Dr. Evans. Keep Captain Maria . posted on any changes.\"\n\nCommander Kael stepped forward to inspect the pod. Commander Kael turned to Captain Maria ., smiling. The bright, sterile lights of the Medical Bay reflected off Commander Kael's smooth, unblemished face. Commander Kael's skin was perfect, revealing a cheek that had never known a wound or a scar.\n\n\"Captain,\" Commander Kael said, patting Commander Kael's empty belt pouch. \"Commander Kael seem to have lost the decryption key. Commander Kael haven't seen the decryption key since yesterday.\"\n\nCaptain Maria . stared at Commander Kael, Captain Maria .'s blood running cold. \"Commander Kael just put the decryption key on the console an hour ago, Commander Kael. And where is Commander Kael's scar?\"\n\nThe man who looked like Commander Kael simply tilted Commander Kael's head, Commander Kael's smile widening. \"yesterday is such a fluid concept, isn't yesterday, Captain Maria .?\"\n",
